  {
   "x": 46.6,
   "y": 50.7,
   "w": 693.6,
   "size": 13.6,
   "flags": 0,
   "text": "The heavenly temple is God’s transcendent dwelling, and people get glimpses of it when they encounter God"
  },
  {
   "x": 46.6,
   "y": 71.1,
   "w": 686.5,
   "size": 13.6,
   "flags": 0,
   "text": "in places where Heaven and Earth overlap. The worldview in these stories shows us the heavenly and earthly"
  },
  {
   "x": 46.6,
   "y": 91.5,
   "w": 670.4,
   "size": 13.6,
   "flags": 0,
   "text": "realms are not completely separate because they overlap at key places and times. We might say these are"
  },
  {
   "x": 46.6,
   "y": 111.9,
   "w": 683.2,
   "size": 13.6,
   "flags": 0,
   "text": "moments of “Heaven on Earth.” Notice that both of these stories are about the foundation of sacred spaces:"
  },
  {
   "x": 46.6,
   "y": 132.2,
   "w": 591.9,
   "size": 13.6,
   "flags": 0,
   "text": "Jacob makes a temple in Bethel, and Moses models the tabernacle after the heavenly temple."
  },
  {
   "x": 46.6,
   "y": 166.2,
   "w": 683.6,
   "size": 13.6,
   "flags": 0,
   "text": "In this worldview, Israel’s tabernacle and temple are a micro-cosmos of all creation, the place where Heaven"
  },
  {
   "x": 46.6,
   "y": 186.6,
   "w": 668.2,
   "size": 13.6,
   "flags": 0,
   "text": "and Earth are one. This explains why these sacred spaces and the stories of their creation are loaded with"
  },
  {
   "x": 46.6,
   "y": 207.0,
   "w": 204.9,
   "size": 13.6,
   "flags": 0,
   "text": "cosmic imagery and symbolism."
